            <name>Jasmonic acid</name>
            <hmdb-id>HMDB0032797</hmdb-id>
            <description>Jasmonic acid is found in apple. Esters are present in Jasminum grandiflorum (royal jasmine) and are responsible for its odour. Jasmonic acid is a member of the jasmonate class of plant hormones. It is biosynthesized from linolenic acid by the octadecanoid pathway.

Jasmonic acid has been shown to exhibit signalling function (PMID 20304987).</description>
